     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-family:tahoma,sans-serif;color:rgb(11,83,148)\">Dear France</div><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-family:tahoma,sans-serif;color:rgb(11,83,148)\"><br></div><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-family:tahoma,sans-serif;color:rgb(11,83,148)\">I am not sure if I understood completely your question. <br></div><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-family:tahoma,sans-serif;color:rgb(11,83,148)\"><br></div><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-family:tahoma,sans-serif;color:rgb(11,83,148)\">parametricTP calculates the parametric version of trophic position, i.e. it should give you the same value for TP if you do the calculation by hand (see the help or <a href=\"https://rdrr.io/cran/tRophicPosition/man/parametricTP.html\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://rdrr.io/cran/tRophicPosition/man/parametricTP.html&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792497490810000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1f65DbDPeWijq7YrDTGzKy\">https://rdrr.io/cran/tRophicPosition/man/parametricTP.html</a>).</div><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-family:tahoma,sans-serif;color:rgb(11,83,148)\"><br></div><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-family:tahoma,sans-serif;color:rgb(11,83,148)\">If you calculate TP with any of the Bayesian models (either several or one species at the same time), the results should not vary, as the calculation doesn&#39;t depend on the rest of species. parametricTP and the Bayesian TP likely will be different.<br></div><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-family:tahoma,sans-serif;color:rgb(11,83,148)\"><br></div><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-family:tahoma,sans-serif;color:rgb(11,83,148)\">If you want, you can send me the raw data, the script you are using to calculate TP and I can tell you what might be wrong, if that&#39;s the case.</div><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-family:tahoma,sans-serif;color:rgb(11,83,148)\"><br></div><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-family:tahoma,sans-serif;color:rgb(11,83,148)\">Cheers</div><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-family:tahoma,sans-serif;color:rgb(11,83,148)\"><br></div><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-family:tahoma,sans-serif;color:rgb(11,83,148)\">Claudio<br></div></div></div><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\"></div>"
    ],
