     "<div class=\"gmail_quote\"><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 0.8ex;border-left:1px solid rgb(204,204,204);padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\">Dear Mr <span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:&quot;Segoe UI&quot;,&quot;Lucida Sans&quot;,sans-serif;font-size:14.16px;background-color:rgb(253,253,253)\">Claudio Quezada,</span><div><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:&quot;Segoe UI&quot;,&quot;Lucida Sans&quot;,sans-serif;font-size:14.16px;background-color:rgb(253,253,253)\"><br></span></div><div><font face=\"Segoe UI, Lucida Sans, sans-serif\" color=\"#000000\"><span style=\"font-size:14.16px;background-color:rgb(253,253,253)\">I am sending you an email as I obtain different TP values when I am working species by species or with different species at the same time.</span></font></div><div><font face=\"Segoe UI, Lucida Sans, sans-serif\" color=\"#000000\"><span style=\"font-size:14.16px;background-color:rgb(253,253,253)\">So I obtained a different TP value with the fonction</span></font><span style=\"background-color:rgb(253,253,253);color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:&quot;Segoe UI&quot;,&quot;Lucida Sans&quot;,sans-serif;font-size:14.16px\"> summary(posterior.grypus) (--&gt; work on one species at the time), and with the fonction Param.TP.Grypus &lt;- parametricTP(Grypus, lambda=3, print=TRUE) (--&gt; more than one species at the time).</span></div><div><span style=\"background-color:rgb(253,253,253);color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:&quot;Segoe UI&quot;,&quot;Lucida Sans&quot;,sans-serif;font-size:14.16px\"><br></span></div><div><span style=\"background-color:rgb(253,253,253);color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:&quot;Segoe UI&quot;,&quot;Lucida Sans&quot;,sans-serif;font-size:14.16px\">Do you know if the values are influenced by the others species in the model?</span></div><div><span style=\"background-color:rgb(253,253,253);color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:&quot;Segoe UI&quot;,&quot;Lucida Sans&quot;,sans-serif;font-size:14.16px\"><br></span></div>